01:22:51,428 --> 01:22:57,428
Rio Lobo is a 1970 American Western film directed and produced by Howard Hawks—his final film—starring John
Wayne, based on a screenplay by Burton Wohl and Leigh Brackett, and composed by Jerry Goldsmith.

11
01:31:08,571 --> 01:31:14,571
The film was shot in Cuernavaca in the Mexican state
of Morelos and in Tucson, Arizona.

12
01:39:25,714 --> 01:39:31,714
It was the third Howard Hawks film to explore the theme of a town sheriff defending his office against belligerent
local outlaws; the others were Rio Bravo (1959) and El Dorado (1966), both also starring John Wayne.

13
01:47:42,857 --> 01:47:48,857
The film explores themes of sheriff, traitor, texas, colonel.
